+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Patch
+([RFC 6902](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)) with its six operations (`add`, `remove`, `replace`,
+`move`, `copy`, `test`) and returns the result as a new value; the input is never mutated, and a patch is
+atomic. It throws an `Error` if the patch is invalid or an operation fails (unresolved path, failed `test`,
+removing the whole document, moving a value into its own child).
+
+```ts
+applyPatch({ foo: "bar" }, [{ op: "add", path: "/baz", value: "qux" }]); // { foo: "bar", baz: "qux" }
+```
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
